<div>
  <p>Hey <%= @seller.name_or_username %>,</p>
  <p>We've improved how refund policies work on Gumroad. You can now set a unique refund policy for each product instead of using a single account-level one. This change is effective immediately, giving you more flexibility for each product's refund terms.</p>
  <p>If you previously set an account-level refund policy, please review your products to ensure the desired policies are applied.</p>
  <p>Soon, we'll be able to process refund requests on your behalf.</p>
  <p>
    You can review your current refund policies or add new ones by editing a product on the <%= link_to("Products", products_url) %> page.<br>
    For more information, see <%= link_to("Set a custom refund policy", "https://gumroad.com/help/article/335-custom-refund-policy") %> help article.
  </p>
</div>
<div>
  <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>
  <h4>What happened to my old product-level refund policies?</h4>
  <p>Your previous product-level refund policies have been automatically restored to your products.</p>
  <h4>Can I keep the account-level refund policy?</h4>
  <p>The account-level refund policy option has been discontinued. We recommend creating specific refund policies for each of your <%= link_to("products", products_url) %>.</p>
  <h4>What happens to existing purchases?</h4>
  <p>Purchases made before this change will keep their original refund policy that was in place at the time of purchase.</p>
</div>
<div>
  <p>More questions? Just reply to this email.</p>
</div>
